  "prompt_text": "Continue the text below with exactly one short, natural, coherent English sentence. Return only the continuation, with no preamble or explanation:\nThis year, scientists after years of research finally discovers a drug that grants eternal youth to its users, making them practically live forever. The effects last a lifetime, and only one dose of the drug is needed for a person to stop aging. People all around the world are given the drug. However, the drug is monitored and only administered to people that are below the age of 20. It was determined that the effects of the drug are not suitable for those older than 20, and that they would still continue to age. Thus, many in the world still found themselves at the mercy of aging, with countless feeling jealous of those that took the drug and would keep their youth forever.\n\nThe world had changed for the better, with many now living enjoyable and carefree lives. It was a peaceful era, that would appear to last forever, just like the users that stopped aging. However, 50 years later, people in the world began to feel strange. The symptoms seemed mild at first for the user.s. They would experience mild nausea, and blurriness, with some feeling dizzy at times. Scientists and doctors concluded it was nothing too serious to worry about, and reassured people that they would be fine. Despite their reassurances, the symptoms soon began intensifying and growing in severity. For some, they experienced intense fevers, others lost sensation in different parts of the body, being paralyzed for hours on end. Many were scared of the symptoms, begging for a cure if it existed, and a treatment to ease their pain.\n\nUltimately scientists and experts around the world could not determine how the side effects manifested. The drug was taken off the market and further research would be made to determine if a cure existed. Their efforts and research had not yet gone underway when the first deaths began being recorded among 